---
layout: none
permalink: /tools.json
---
{
  "$schema": "https://tools.apievangelist.com/tool.schema.json",
  "name": "API Evangelist Tools",
  "description": "Open source tooling for the specifications that describe, secure and ship APIs — with the licensing, invocation semantics and use cases an AI agent needs to actually employ them.",
  "url": "https://tools.apievangelist.com",
  "documentation": "https://tools.apievangelist.com/reference/",
  "vocabulary": "https://tools.apievangelist.com/roles.json",
  "schema": "https://tools.apievangelist.com/tool.schema.json",
  "standards": "https://standards.apievangelist.com",
  "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
{%- comment -%}
  The store is the UNION of two catalogues, and every entry is published. `sources` on each
  entry says which one it came from, because they carry different guarantees:

    specification-catalog — the repository was resolved live against the GitHub API, the
                            license was read from it, and it is bound to a specification
                            with a role. Only these carry license/repository/agent blocks.
    demand-corpus         — it is in the insights tool vocabulary, so it carries a
                            companyCount and radarRing from the job corpus.

  Most entries are one or the other. An entry in both is a tool we have read AND measured.
  Filter on `sources` rather than assuming every entry has a license or a count.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign items = site.store | sort: "title" -%}
{%- assign spec_tools = site.store | where_exp: "t", "t.specifications" -%}
{%- assign demand_tools = site.store | where_exp: "t", "t.companyCountQuarter" -%}
  "count": {{ items | size }},
  "counts": {
    "total": {{ items | size }},
    "specificationCatalog": {{ spec_tools | size }},
    "demandCorpus": {{ demand_tools | size }},
    "note": "Entries carry `sources`. Only specification-catalog entries have a verified license, repository and specification bindings; only demand-corpus entries have a companyCount. See /reference/."
  },
  "tools": [
{%- for t in items %}
    {
      "slug": {{ t.slug | default: t.title | jsonify }},
      "title": {{ t.title | jsonify }},
      "url": "https://tools.apievangelist.com{{ t.url }}",
      "sources": [{% if t.specifications %}"specification-catalog"{% endif %}{% if t.specifications and t.companyCountQuarter %}, {% endif %}{% if t.companyCountQuarter %}"demand-corpus"{% endif %}],
      "description": {{ t.description | strip_newlines | jsonify }}
      {%- if t.website %},
      "website": {{ t.website | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.repository %},
      "repository": {{ t.repository | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.license %},
      "license": {{ t.license | jsonify }},
      "openSource": {{ t.openSource | default: false }},
      "licenseSource": {{ t.licenseSource | default: "unresolved" | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.stars %},
      "stars": {{ t.stars }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.lastCommit %},
      "lastCommit": {{ t.lastCommit | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.archived %},
      "archived": true{% endif %}
      {%- if t.companyCountQuarter %},
      "companyCount": {{ t.companyCount | default: 0 }},
      "companyCountQuarter": {{ t.companyCountQuarter | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.nameCollision %},
      "nameCollision": true,
      "nameCollisionNote": {{ t.nameCollisionNote | strip_newlines | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.radarRing %},
      "radarRing": {{ t.radarRing | jsonify }}{% endif %}
      {%- if t.specifications %},
      "specifications": [
        {%- for s in t.specifications %}
        {
          "slug": {{ s.slug | jsonify }},
          "name": {{ s.name | jsonify }},
          "role": {{ s.role | jsonify }},
          "url": "https://standards.apievangelist.com/store/{{ s.slug }}/"
          {%- if s.also %},
          "also": {{ s.also | jsonify }}{% endif %}
          {%- if s.produces %},
          "produces": {{ s.produces | jsonify }}{% endif %}
        }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
        {%- endfor %}
      ]{% endif %}
      {%- if t.agent %},
      "agent": {
        {%- if t.agent.interfaces %}
        "interfaces": {{ t.agent.interfaces | jsonify }},{% endif %}
        {%- if t.agent.install %}
        "install": {{ t.agent.install | jsonify }},{% endif %}
        {%- if t.agent.invoke %}
        "invoke": {{ t.agent.invoke | jsonify }},{% endif %}
        {%- if t.agent.consumes %}
        "consumes": {{ t.agent.consumes | jsonify }},{% endif %}
        {%- if t.agent.emits %}
        "emits": {{ t.agent.emits | jsonify }},{% endif %}
        "deterministic": {{ t.agent.deterministic | default: false }},
        "offline": {{ t.agent.offline | default: false }},
        "mutates": {{ t.agent.mutates | default: false }},
        "credentials": {{ t.agent.credentials | default: false }}
      }{% endif %}
      {%- if t.useCases %},
      "useCases": [
        {%- for u in t.useCases %}
        {
          "task": {{ u.task | strip_newlines | jsonify }}
          {%- if u.surface %},
          "surface": {{ u.surface | jsonify }}{% endif %}
          {%- if u.note %},
          "note": {{ u.note | strip_newlines | jsonify }}{% endif %}
        }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
        {%- endfor %}
      ]{% endif %}
      {%- if t.tags %},
      "tags": {{ t.tags | jsonify }}{% endif %}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
  ]
}
